messages:
maria: Quick check — I'm about to merge a Terraform change that reduces serviceAccount projected token TTL from 24h to 6h and adds annotation `redwood.io/sa-token-renewal: "enabled"` on workloads to trigger refresh. PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/infra/pull/4820 Anyone aware of services that require long-lived k8s tokens?

jon: FYI batch-worker and offline-processor might be sensitive; they run cron pods for >12h jobs.

priya: We use ExternalSecrets on a few services — the controller reads projected tokens via projected-volume. Make sure the Secret refresh controller tolerates shorter TTLs. Which controller version is in staging?

maria: staging has external-secrets v0.6.2. Change I'm planning (snippet):
```
resource "kubernetes_service_account" "app" {
  metadata {
    name = "svc-app"
    annotations = {
      "redwood.io/sa-token-renewal" = "enabled"
    }
  }
}

resource "kubernetes_secret" "sa-token" {
  metadata { name = "svc-app-token" }
  data = { token = base64encode(...) }
}
```

and in terraform vars: `sa_token_ttl = "6h"`

and I'll also update the ExternalSecret CRD to set `refreshInterval: 2m` for canaries.

andrew: Can we add a canary label and only apply to one namespace first? Then watch `kube-apiserver` audit logs for token warnings.

maria: Good idea — will patch staging via `terraform apply -target=kubernetes_service_account.app -var=env=staging` and create a small canary namespace `sa-ttl-canary`.

sre-bot: CI plan: infra PR 4820 — plan succeeded on staging workspace (:white_check_mark:)

priya: After you apply, please run `kubectl get pods -n sa-ttl-canary -o jsonpath="{.items[*].metadata.name}"` and check ExternalSecrets controller logs for errors.

maria: On it. Expect apply in ~10min, will post results.

deploy-bot: terraform apply complete in staging for targets: kubernetes_service_account.app (:rocket:)

maria: applied to staging, canary created `sa-ttl-canary`. No immediate failures in logs. Started a 8h background job in canary to validate long-running workloads.

jon: Thanks — I'll run the overnight batch in canary and report back.

priya: If no issues by tomorrow morning, approve for canary roll to 10% of namespaces. :thumbsup:

maria: pinging @eng-oncall so they see the rollout window.

andrew: Approving the change from infra side. :white_check_mark:

maria: Thanks all — will keep this thread updated.
